    "body": "fix on issue/1909-bore-wide-hole-tests · PR #1912 · pinned by detect_holes_note_tests::detect_holes_on_a_bore_op_stores_the_wide_through_hole_and_names_the_one_past_the_ring_budget, detect_holes_note_tests::detect_holes_on_a_bore_op_with_only_a_hole_past_the_ring_budget_is_refused · merges when reviewed\n\nCause: PR #1839 (#1566) lets Bore clear a wide hole with concentric rings. Detect holes now keeps the Ø74.3 hole, as the design says. The tests were stale, and the product is correct. No refusal was lost: a hole past the 4096-ring budget is still refused. The 78 s time is not the cost of the tests. Locally each test ends in about 0.02 s.\n",
